# 🍈 Melon Variety Selection Trial (2022) – Field Experiment & Statistical Analysis

## 📌 Project Overview

This project presents an agronomic field trial conducted to evaluate early-season melon varieties under open-field conditions. The objective was to identify high-performing pre-commercial varieties suitable for market introduction.

The study combines **field experimentation**, **data analysis**, and **statistical modeling** to support decision-making in varietal selection.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

* Evaluate the field performance of pre-commercial melon varieties (PLC5)
* Compare candidate varieties to commercial controls
* Identify 1–2 varieties with strong agronomic and commercial potential

---

## 🧪 Experimental Design

* Total plants: 321
* Plot size: 7 plants per plot
* Design: Randomized block design
* Replicates: 3
* Varieties tested: 20+ (including controls)

### Factors studied:

* Variety
* Company (e.g. Syngenta, Clause)
* Variety type (Control vs test)

---

## 📊 Data Collection

Data were collected using multiple tools:

* Field observations
* Drone imagery
* Video recordings
* Tablets and Excel sheets

---

## 📈 Data Analysis

Data processing and statistical analysis were performed using:

* Microsoft Excel
* Analysis of Variance (ANOVA)
* Newman-Keuls post-hoc test (5% significance level)

The analysis focused on:

### Quantitative traits:

* Fruit count per plot
* Yield performance
* Average fruit weight

### Qualitative traits:

* Waste percentage
* Fruit defects (cracks, rot, deformities)
* Sugar content (Brix)

---

## 🔍 Key Findings

* Several varieties showed strong early yield performance (e.g. MC24908, MC26015, MC26097)
* Some varieties combined high yield with acceptable fruit quality
* Trade-offs were observed between yield and waste rate
* Two varieties were shortlisted for further comparison with commercial controls

---

